course: dictionary
lesson: 12344
title: Crafty: clever tricks
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Crafty usually means clever at getting what you want by tricks and secret plans. Another word for it is sly. The clues are often in the actions of the character. «The crafty fox pretended to be a friend so the crow would drop her cheese.» The fox pretended, so it was tricking the crow, which means crafty is about clever tricks.
explain: Ask yourself: is the character planning something secret? «She gave him a crafty look, as if she had a secret plan.» A look that hides a plan shows that crafty means sly and clever, not just skilful.
explain: Crafty can also mean good at making things by hand. This is an informal meaning, so you will hear it in everyday talk more than in stories. «Dad is crafty and built a birdhouse from old wood.» Here the clue is built, so crafty means skilled at making.
explain: Always check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If «sly» fits and makes sense, you have probably found the right meaning.
fact: Crafty means clever at getting what you want by tricks and secret plans; sly is a close synonym.
fact: In fables, the fox is often crafty, as when it tricks the crow into dropping her cheese.
fact: «Toad made a crafty escape by dressing up as an old washerwoman.» Crafty shows that the escape was planned in a clever, sneaky way.
fact: Informal meaning: crafty can mean good at making things by hand, as in «She is crafty with paper and glue.»
fact: The same word can have two meanings, so read the clues in the sentence to choose the right one.
exercise: «The crafty fox pretended to be a friend so the crow would drop her cheese.» What does crafty mean here? | Loud and noisy | Wet and grey | Very hungry | *Clever at tricking to get what you want
exercise: «She gave him a crafty look, as if she had a secret plan.» Which word is the best synonym for crafty here? | Sleepy | *Sly | Generous | Cheerful
exercise: Grandma says, «I am crafty with a needle; I make quilts and cards.» What does crafty mean here? | Frightened of needles | Full of tricks and lies | Very old | *Good at making things by hand
test: «Toad made a crafty escape by dressing up as an old washerwoman.» Which word in the sentence shows the trick? | escape | Toad | made | *dressing up
test: «Dad is crafty and built a birdhouse from old wood.» What does crafty mean here? | Sly and tricky | *Good at making things by hand | Afraid of wood | Very tired
exam: «The crafty plan worked, and nobody saw the trick.» Which meaning fits best? | Very loud | Slow and tired | *Clever and sly | Made of wool
